        <body>
            <div xml:id="d405">

                <pb facs="0680" n="1640" xml:id="pg1640"/>

                <head>No. 1118.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Scott to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Carácas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 30, 1887</date>.
                        (Received December 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 204.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your No. 136, in relation to the closing of the ports of Venezuela against
                    Curaçao, and to state that I will avail myself of the first opportunity to make
                    known to the Venezuelan Government, through Dr. Urbaneja, minister of exterior
                    relations, your views on this subject, as expressed in your No. 126, and dated
                    Washington, September 22, 1887, thus carrying out the instructions embraced in
                    your No. 136.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles L. Scott.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
